# Shakshuka

Based on [https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/…](https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014721-shakshuka-with-feta) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251214090115/https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014721-shakshuka-with-feta))

{ rating="3" image="shakshuka.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 3 Tbsp [extra-virgin olive oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 large [onion]{ ing="onion" }, halved and thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 large [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, seeded and thinly sliced
- [ ] 3 [garlic cloves]{ ing="garlic-cloves" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [sweet paprika]{ ing="sweet-paprika" }
- [ ] 1/8 tsp [ground cayenne]{ ing="ground-cayenne" }, or to taste
- [ ] 1 (28-oz) can [whole plum tomatoes]{ ing="whole-plum-tomatoes" } with their juices, coarsely chopped
- [ ] 3/4 tsp [kosher salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" }, plus more as needed
- [ ] 1/4 tsp [black pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }, plus more as needed
- [ ] 5 oz [feta]{ ing="feta" }, crumbled (about 1.25 cups; or drop spoonfuls of cottage cheese alongside the feta)
- [ ] 6 large [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] [Chopped cilantro]{ ing="chopped-cilantro" }, for serving
- [ ] [Hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }, for serving

## Recipe

1. Heat oven to 375F
1. Heat [oil]{ ing="extra-virgin-olive-oil" } in a large skillet over medium-low. Add [onion]{ ing="onion" } and [bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }. Cook gently until very soft, about 20 minutes
1. Add garlic and cook until tender, 1 to 2 minutes; stir in [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [paprika]{ ing="sweet-paprika" } and [cayenne]{ ing="ground-cayenne" }, and cook 1 minute
1. Pour in [tomatoes]{ ing="whole-plum-tomatoes" } and season with 3/4 tsp [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and 1/4 tsp [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }; simmer until tomatoes have thickened, about 10 minutes
1. Taste and add more [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" } if needed
1. Stir in crumbled [feta]{ ing="feta" }
1. Gently crack [eggs]{ ing="egg" } into skillet over [tomatoes]{ ing="whole-plum-tomatoes" }. Season eggs with [salt]{ ing="kosher-salt" } and [pepper]{ ing="black-pepper" }
1. Transfer skillet to oven and bake until [eggs]{ ing="egg" } are just set, 7 to 10 minutes. Sprinkle with [cilantro]{ ing="chopped-cilantro" } and serve with [hot sauce]{ ing="hot-sauce" }
